@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+# SphereOpt 0.9.3 current-game update
+
+Unofficial compatibility update based on Andy O'Neal's SphereOpt 0.9.2.
+Assessed against Dyson Sphere Program 0.10.35.29151, Steam build 25955035,
+Unity 2022.3.62f3c1. Requires BepInEx 5.4.17 or a compatible installation.
+
+This update batches eligible Dyson shell layers. Vanilla continues to render
+nodes, frames, painting overlays and layers outside the supported shader domain.
+The game's GPU profiler uses the complete vanilla path so its counters remain
+meaningful. Direct3D 11, shader model 5, instancing and texture arrays are required.
+
+The author’s old custom node/frame shaders and culling kernel have confirmed
+correctness defects. This update does not activate them. Their source is retained
+for future development. The original mod's advertised node/frame LOD and culling
+are therefore not features of this update.
+
+Changes include typed access to current private game fields, current-game builds,
+semantic painting updates, style synchronization, post-construction progress,
+per-layer stencil materials, safe initialization and fallback, and bounded shell
+pool storage across deletion and regeneration. Original game materials remain
+available for fallback. Renderer ownership uses actual sphere/layer objects.
+
+The repaired shell shader supports construction progress and pole geometry.
+Its exact bytes are required at startup; an old or mismatched bundle disables
+the optimization and leaves vanilla available. See `SHADER_PROVENANCE.json` for
+the source/program identities and compilation/serialization checks. The
+[DSPMods workspace](https://github.com/rk-gamemods/DSPMods) contains the research
+and final validation record.
+
+Build and tests do not establish visual parity or a performance gain. No game
+launch, GPU rendering test, save test or benchmark was performed during this
+offline update. The original shell shader also contains lighting approximations.
+This is a compatibility candidate rather than a measured performance release.
+
+## Build and validate
+
+The owning DSPMods workspace verifies a private snapshot of the installed game
+before building. It never redistributes the game's DLLs or reconstructed source.
+
+```powershell
+dotnet build tools/SphereOpt.OfflineBuild -c Release
+dotnet run --project external/SphereOpt/tests/SphereOpt.Tests -c Release
+dotnet run --project external/SphereOpt/tests/SphereOpt.LayerTests -c Release
+dotnet run --project external/SphereOpt/tests/SphereOpt.RenderTests -c Release
+py -3 tools/check_sphereopt_shaders.py
+py -3 tools/game_snapshot.py check-mod .local/build/SphereOpt/SphereOpt.dll
+```
+
+Run these commands from DSPMods. The standalone project also accepts
+`-p:DSPManagedDir=<captured-managed-directory>`; redirect its output and
+`BaseIntermediateOutputPath` outside the clone. A default build uses the
+upstream reference packages and is not the installed-game validation route.
+
+## Installation
+
+The local package contains `SphereOpt.dll` and `sphereopt-bundle`. Both belong
+together in one BepInEx plugins folder. Do not install this alongside another
+SphereOpt DLL. This workspace has not installed the package or changed the game.
+
+Preserve `LICENSE.txt` and `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt` when distributing a package.
+Upstream source and historical release notes remain in `README.md`.
