+++ b/tests/SphereOpt.RenderTests/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+# Render patch tests
+
+Run from the DSPMods workspace with the .NET 8 runtime and a compatible SDK:
+
+```powershell
+dotnet run --project external/SphereOpt/tests/SphereOpt.RenderTests/SphereOpt.RenderTests.csproj --configuration Release
+```
+
+The project links the actual `Patch_DysonSphereSegmentRenderer.cs` and
+`ShellCursorRewriter.cs`. It invokes `BeforeDraw`, `RenderShellCursor`, and
+`AfterDraw` through reflection. It does not copy their context implementation.
+HarmonyX is locked to 2.5.5. The shared test `Directory.Build.props` puts
+intermediate files and binaries under `.local/build/SphereOptTests/`, with a
+separate directory for this project.
+
+The exhaustive mask case covers all 59,049 combinations of ineligible,
+eligible but unsubmitted, and submitted states across ten layers. Other cases
+cover successful callback timing, exact sphere/layer identities and recreation,
+nested calls and bypassed nested calls, render-place/profiler/inactive guards,
+missing player/game data, zero preparation masks, preparation/submission
+failures, exception cleanup, repeated cleanup, and thread-local context isolation.
+A synthetic emitted method also runs the actual transpiler and getter together.
+Guard precedence cases also combine bypasses with a missing sphere/player.
+
+`PrepareFrame`, `RenderShells`, plugin disable/release effects, and game data
+are fakes. The harness does not execute actual eligibility/readiness checks,
+native rendering, shaders, GPU submission, or resource teardown. Its exception
+cases execute a controlled original failure with the actual finalizer in
+`finally`, and verify the finalizer's Harmony attributes and void return
+contract. They do not install or execute a Harmony detour.
+Nested cases prove patch-context restoration. The actual renderer stores a
+shared `PreparedMask`; these fakes cannot establish that same-sphere renderer
+reentry preserves an outer invocation's prepared selection.
+
+An optional captured-IL check reads a captured assembly as PE metadata:
+
+```powershell
+dotnet run --project external/SphereOpt/tests/SphereOpt.RenderTests/SphereOpt.RenderTests.csproj --configuration Release -- --captured-assembly '<captured snapshot>/Managed/Assembly-CSharp.dll'
+```
+
+That check passes the captured method's opcodes and metadata operands through
+the actual rewriter, using `FieldInfo` wrappers identified by module MVID and
+field token. It independently requires the first load to feed a remainder and
+the second to feed a backward less-than branch. The production rewriter itself
+checks only the number of loads. The check verifies every other
+instruction and operand remains unchanged. It prints the assembly SHA-256 and
+method token. The assembly is never runtime-loaded or executed. Branch/switch
+operands remain opaque Cecil metadata; this check does not reconstruct Harmony
+labels/exception blocks or certify executable full-game IL. Captured inputs
+remain outside this test directory.
+
+The final isolation check rejects loaded or referenced game, plugin, Unity,
+and BepInEx assemblies. No Unity stub is needed because the linked patch and
+rewriter do not reference Unity APIs.
+
+Run the focused regression counterfactuals with:
+
+```powershell
+py -3 external/SphereOpt/tests/SphereOpt.RenderTests/verify_counterfactuals.py
+```
+
+The script generates three mutated patch copies under `.local/build`, uses
+the same dependency lock, and requires each to reach failing harness assertions.
+The mutations clear completed callbacks on failure, suppress prepared layers
+before callbacks, or remove exact layer identity. Production files remain
+unchanged. Full failure logs stay beside the generated projects.
